{"slug":"hasura-deployment","wpId":6405,"title":"Hasura – Deployment","category":"hasura","categories":["hasura"],"tags":[],"date":"2020-03-17T01:10:49","modified":"2021-11-19T01:19:36","excerpt":"Deploying or Running Hasura on AWS ECS Fargate Create a Task Definition Use the right hasura docker image Environment variables must be present Host port and Container port must be the same to work. I tried having container port different from host port and that did not work for me Size Leave…","url":"/hasura/hasura-deployment","contentHtml":"<div class=\"boldgrid-section\">\n<div class=\"container\">\n<div class=\"row\">\n<div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12 col-sm-12\">\n<h1 class=\"\">Deploying or Running Hasura on AWS ECS Fargate</h1>\n<h2 class=\"\" id=\"create-a-task-definition\">Create a Task Definition</h2>\n<ol class=\"\">\n<li>Use the right hasura docker image<img alt=\"\" class=\"aligncenter size-large wp-image-7289\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"664\" loading=\"lazy\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" src=\"https://d2q2snz6diubfd.cloudfront.net/media/2020/03/Screen-Shot-2021-11-18-at-6.03.58-PM.png\" srcset=\"https://d2q2snz6diubfd.cloudfront.net/media/2020/03/Screen-Shot-2021-11-18-at-6.03.58-PM.png 1024w, https://d2q2snz6diubfd.cloudfront.net/media/2020/03/Screen-Shot-2021-11-18-at-6.03.58-PM.png 300w, https://d2q2snz6diubfd.cloudfront.net/media/2020/03/Screen-Shot-2021-11-18-at-6.03.58-PM.png 768w, https://d2q2snz6diubfd.cloudfront.net/media/2020/03/Screen-Shot-2021-11-18-at-6.03.58-PM.png 250w, https://d2q2snz6diubfd.cloudfront.net/media/2020/03/Screen-Shot-2021-11-18-at-6.03.58-PM.png 550w, https://d2q2snz6diubfd.cloudfront.net/media/2020/03/Screen-Shot-2021-11-18-at-6.03.58-PM.png 800w, https://d2q2snz6diubfd.cloudfront.net/media/2020/03/Screen-Shot-2021-11-18-at-6.03.58-PM.png 278w, https://d2q2snz6diubfd.cloudfront.net/media/2020/03/Screen-Shot-2021-11-18-at-6.03.58-PM.png 463w, https://d2q2snz6diubfd.cloudfront.net/media/2020/03/Screen-Shot-2021-11-18-at-6.03.58-PM.png 771w, https://d2q2snz6diubfd.cloudfront.net/media/2020/03/Screen-Shot-2021-11-18-at-6.03.58-PM.png 1468w\" width=\"1024\"/></li>\n<li>Environment variables must be present</li>\n<li>Host port and Container port must be the same to work. I tried having container port different from host port and that did not work for me</li>\n<li>Size<br/>\n<img alt=\"\" class=\"aligncenter size-large wp-image-7290\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"336\" loading=\"lazy\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" src=\"https://d2q2snz6diubfd.cloudfront.net/media/2020/03/Screen-Shot-2021-11-18-at-6.06.14-PM.png\" srcset=\"https://d2q2snz6diubfd.cloudfront.net/media/2020/03/Screen-Shot-2021-11-18-at-6.06.14-PM.png 1024w, https://d2q2snz6diubfd.cloudfront.net/media/2020/03/Screen-Shot-2021-11-18-at-6.06.14-PM.png 300w, https://d2q2snz6diubfd.cloudfront.net/media/2020/03/Screen-Shot-2021-11-18-at-6.06.14-PM.png 768w, https://d2q2snz6diubfd.cloudfront.net/media/2020/03/Screen-Shot-2021-11-18-at-6.06.14-PM.png 1536w, https://d2q2snz6diubfd.cloudfront.net/media/2020/03/Screen-Shot-2021-11-18-at-6.06.14-PM.png 2048w, https://d2q2snz6diubfd.cloudfront.net/media/2020/03/Screen-Shot-2021-11-18-at-6.06.14-PM.png 250w, https://d2q2snz6diubfd.cloudfront.net/media/2020/03/Screen-Shot-2021-11-18-at-6.06.14-PM.png 550w, https://d2q2snz6diubfd.cloudfront.net/media/2020/03/Screen-Shot-2021-11-18-at-6.06.14-PM.png 800w, https://d2q2snz6diubfd.cloudfront.net/media/2020/03/Screen-Shot-2021-11-18-at-6.06.14-PM.png 549w, https://d2q2snz6diubfd.cloudfront.net/media/2020/03/Screen-Shot-2021-11-18-at-6.06.14-PM.png 915w, https://d2q2snz6diubfd.cloudfront.net/media/2020/03/Screen-Shot-2021-11-18-at-6.06.14-PM.png 1526w\" width=\"1024\"/></li>\n<li>Leave “Operating system family” alone.</li>\n<li>Leave entrypoint or any command alone.</li>\n<li>Make sure that the ecs execution role has previliges to access other aws parties your app needs. Things such as secret manager, sqs, email, etc.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2 class=\"\" id=\"create-a-service-using-your-task-definition\">Create a Service using your Task Definition</h2>\n<ol class=\"\">\n<li>Fill in the Service details</li>\n<li>For security group, create a new security and make sure that group has access to and from database, third party APIs, or other aws services that call your service</li>\n<li>Make sure you only include AZ zones that are allowed by your load balancer.</li>\n<li>Add load balancer</li>\n<li>Add health check /ping</li>\n<li>Allow your server to boot up and be healthy before load balancer starts checking for its health</li>\n</ol>\n<p> </p>\n<p class=\"\"> </p>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n","toc":[{"id":"create-a-task-definition","text":"Create a Task Definition","level":2},{"id":"create-a-service-using-your-task-definition","text":"Create a Service using your Task Definition","level":2}],"wordCount":166,"readingMinutes":1,"status":"published"}